    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Calvinism</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>calvinismo</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The Christian religious tradition based upon the doctrines and forms of Christian practice of several Protestant reformers, especially John Calvin, in contrast to Catholicism, Lutheranism, Anabaptism, and Arminianism. One distinctive trait of the system is its Augustinian doctrine of predestination, which teaches that God has elected some for salvation, apart from anything they do or believe.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
